@{
    // What the company sells, published. Every service below is a thing the platform
    // records, not an aspiration: if a line here had no screen or table behind it, it
    // would not be on the page.
    Layout = "_LandingLayout";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Services";
}

<section class="lnd-section lnd-section--top" id="services">
    <div class="lnd-wrap">
        <div class="lnd-doc__masthead">
            <p class="lnd-kicker">Verichat Quality Projects &middot; Services</p>
            <h1 class="lnd-doc__title">Eight things, and one account that ties them together.</h1>
            <p class="lnd-doc__standfirst">
                Verichat supplies clinical consumables and equipment, buys stock on a
                client's behalf, moves it, installs it, keeps it calibrated and turns up when
                it fails. The services below are usually quoted as a package, because the
                ward that runs out of giving sets and the theatre whose light head is out of
                calibration are the same client with the same file.
            </p>

            <dl class="lnd-doc__meta">
                <div>
                    <dt>Quoted</dt>
                    <dd>Supply and service together, against one lead time</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Answered</dt>
                    <dd>Within twenty-four hours of an enquiry arriving</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Billed</dt>
                    <dd>Against the quotation the client accepted in the portal</dd>
                </div>
            </dl>
        </div>

        <div class="lnd-doc__glance">
            <div class="lnd-doc__glance-item">
                <b>Supply</b>
                <span>Consumables, equipment, protective wear and teaching stock</span>
            </div>
            <div class="lnd-doc__glance-item">
                <b>Buy</b>
                <span>Purchase orders written against named suppliers when your shelf runs low</span>
            </div>
            <div class="lnd-doc__glance-item">
                <b>Move</b>
                <span>Tracked consignments, cold-chain where the product needs it</span>
            </div>
            <div class="lnd-doc__glance-item">
                <b>Keep</b>
                <span>Installation, calibration, preventive visits and fault response</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ THE SERVICES ============ -->
<section class="lnd-section" id="what-we-do">
    <div class="lnd-wrap">
        <div class="lnd-head" data-reveal>
            <p class="lnd-kicker">01 &mdash; The services</p>
            <h2>From the shelf to the service calendar.</h2>
            <p>
                Each of these is something a client can ask for and a Verichat role is
                accountable for delivering. The people who work them are named on the
                <a href="/about">company profile</a>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="lnd-splits">
            <div class="lnd-split" data-reveal>
                <span class="lnd-split__media">
                    <img src="/images/landing/service-consumables.jpg"
                         alt="Shelves of sealed clinical consumables - cartons of giving sets, dressings and surgical masks - in a store cupboard."
                         loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </span>
                <div class="lnd-split__body">
                    <p class="lnd-split__num">01 &mdash; Consumables</p>
                    <h3>Clinical consumables, held above a reorder point.</h3>
                    <p>
                        Giving sets, IV and infusion lines, dressings, syringes, gloves and
                        surgical masks, stocked in the pack sizes a ward actually gets through
                        rather than the case size a distributor prefers. Every line is
                        lot-coded, and the reorder point is a number in the system, not a guess
                        made when the shelf looks empty.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="lnd-points">
                        <li>Batch and lot recorded against the delivery it left on.</li>
                        <li>Reorder points per item, so a shortage is flagged before it is a crisis.</li>
                        <li>Box, carton and ward-level pack sizes quoted side by side.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="lnd-roles"><span>Hospitals</span><span>Clinics</span><span>Day units</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="lnd-split" data-reveal>
                <span class="lnd-split__media">
                    <img src="/images/landing/service-equipment.jpg"
                         alt="Rehabilitation and ward equipment arranged in a delivery bay - a folding aluminium wheelchair, bed cradle and transfer trolley."
                         loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </span>
                <div class="lnd-split__body">
                    <p class="lnd-split__num">02 &mdash; Equipment</p>
                    <h3>Equipment and mobility aid, delivered ready to use.</h3>
                    <p>
                        Wheelchairs and walking frames, bed cradles and transfer aids,
                        examination and theatre furniture, training mannequins and laboratory
                        benches. Bulky items go out assembled and fitted on site where the
                        client asks for it, and the serial number of the unit that arrived is
                        written into the register the service calendar works from.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="lnd-points">
                        <li>Assembly and on-site fitting before the vehicle leaves.</li>
                        <li>Serial number, warranty start and calibration date recorded on the asset.</li>
                        <li>Spare parts quoted against the same asset, not a generic model name.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="lnd-roles"><span>Rehabilitation</span><span>Wards</span><span>Laboratories</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="lnd-split" data-reveal>
                <span class="lnd-split__media">
                    <img src="/images/landing/sector-education.jpg"
                         alt="A teaching laboratory with training mannequins on trolleys and racks of lab coats along the wall."
                         loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </span>
                <div class="lnd-split__body">
                    <p class="lnd-split__num">03 &mdash; Institutional</p>
                    <h3>Protective wear and teaching stock, by the size run.</h3>
                    <p>
                        Lab coats, coveralls, safety boots, high-visibility wear, gloves and
                        eye protection for mines and factories; and the consumables a teaching
                        laboratory gets through in a term. Institutions order these by size
                        distribution rather than by unit, so they are stocked and invoiced
                        that way - with the same reorder alert behind them as anything else.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="lnd-points">
                        <li>Size runs held as one line, so a cohort is issued in one delivery.</li>
                        <li>Minimum performance standards stated on the quotation.</li>
                        <li>Reissued each intake against the department's own forecast.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="lnd-roles"><span>Colleges</span><span>Mines</span><span>Factories</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="lnd-split" data-reveal>
                <span class="lnd-split__media">
                    <img src="/images/landing/service-procurement.jpg"
                         alt="A procurement desk with a purchase order, supplier quotations and a laptop showing a stock alert."
                         loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </span>
                <div class="lnd-split__body">
                    <p class="lnd-split__num">04 &mdash; Procurement</p>
                    <h3>We buy it for you, and the order is written down.</h3>
                    <p>
                        A client that does not want to run a purchasing function can let the
                        threshold do it: stock falls below the reorder point, an alert reaches
                        our procurement desk, and accepting that alert writes a real purchase
                        order against a named supplier. The client sees the consignment that
                        came out of it, not the paperwork behind it.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="lnd-points">
                        <li>Supplier records, lead times and prices held per item.</li>
                        <li>Purchase orders raised from an alert rather than from a phone call.</li>
                        <li>Client-side visibility of what has been ordered on their account.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="lnd-roles"><span>Procurement managers</span><span>Hospital stores</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="lnd-split" data-reveal>
                <span class="lnd-split__media">
                    <img src="/images/landing/dispatch-cold-chain.jpg"
                         alt="A navy transit case and sealed sterile packs staged on a loading dock at dusk beside a delivery vehicle."
                         loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </span>
                <div class="lnd-split__body">
                    <p class="lnd-split__num">05 &mdash; Logistics</p>
                    <h3>Delivery with a number the client can follow.</h3>
                    <p>
                        Consignments leave Harare with a tracking reference and a status
                        history, so a store clerk checking whether the order is coming and a
                        Verichat dispatcher answering the same question are reading the same
                        record. Temperature-sensitive product moves in cold-chain packaging with
                        the handling instructions on the carton.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="lnd-points">
                        <li>Tracking reference issued per consignment, readable by the client.</li>
                        <li>Status history written as it changes, not reconstructed afterwards.</li>
                        <li>Cold-chain packaging and handling noted against the line.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="lnd-roles"><span>Site clinics</span><span>Stores</span><span>Depots</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="lnd-split" data-reveal>
                <span class="lnd-split__media">
                    <img src="/images/landing/service-calibration.jpg"
                         alt="A biomedical engineer calibrating a patient monitor on a trolley, with a logbook open beside it."
                         loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </span>
                <div class="lnd-split__body">
                    <p class="lnd-split__num">06 &mdash; Service</p>
                    <h3>Installation, calibration and a preventive calendar.</h3>
                    <p>
                        Equipment is installed against a checklist and then stays attached to
                        us. Warranty expiry and the next calibration date belong to the asset
                        record, so a unit due for service appears on a schedule rather than
                        failing mid-clinic. Preventive visits are planned against those dates.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="lnd-points">
                        <li>Commissioning checklist recorded at installation.</li>
                        <li>Calibration and warranty dates carried by the asset itself.</li>
                        <li>Preventive visits scheduled from those dates, per client.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="lnd-roles"><span>Theatres</span><span>Monitoring</span><span>Laboratories</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="lnd-split" data-reveal>
                <span class="lnd-split__media">
                    <img src="/images/landing/service-field-engineer.jpg"
                         alt="A field support engineer with a tool case signing a service report on a ward corridor wall."
                         loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </span>
                <div class="lnd-split__body">
                    <p class="lnd-split__num">07 &mdash; Fault response</p>
                    <h3>A ticket, a deadline and an engineer who can close it.</h3>
                    <p>
                        A fault raised in the portal or the mobile app becomes a ticket with a
                        response deadline attached to it. Tickets route to the person who can
                        actually fix the class of problem, escalation is recorded when a
                        deadline is missed, and a resolution is not accepted without the notes
                        that say what was done.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="lnd-points">
                        <li>Priority and SLA set when the ticket is raised, not negotiated later.</li>
                        <li>Escalation level recorded against the ticket when a target slips.</li>
                        <li>Client can see the status and the resolution notes on their own asset.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="lnd-roles"><span>Field support</span><span>Clinical engineering</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="lnd-split" data-reveal>
                <span class="lnd-split__media">
                    <img src="/images/landing/service-portal.jpg"
                         alt="A tablet showing a client catalogue and a phone showing an order cart, both on a dark navy interface."
                         loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </span>
                <div class="lnd-split__body">
                    <p class="lnd-split__num">08 &mdash; The portal</p>
                    <h3>Ordering and looking things up, from either door.</h3>
                    <p>
                        Clients get an account: a catalogue scoped to them, quotations they can
                        accept or decline, their own deliveries and their own tickets. A mobile
                        application carries the same catalogue to the people standing in the
                        store cupboard, and queues an order when there is no signal to send it.
                        Staff work from the same records with different screens.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="lnd-points">
                        <li>A portal account sees only its own orders, quotes and deliveries.</li>
                        <li>Only the screens your role holds are offered to you.</li>
                        <li>Password reset, email confirmation and a help route when it goes wrong.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="lnd-roles"><span>Client users</span><span>Students</span><span>Staff</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="lnd-callout" data-reveal>
            <p>
                <strong>What this page is not.</strong> It is not a price list, and nothing on
                it is an offer. Prices, lead times and the scope of a service agreement are set
                against a specific client's stock levels and site conditions, and they are only
                binding when they appear on a numbered quotation. <a href="/contact">Ask for a
                quotation</a> and you get that document, not an estimate typed into an email.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<hr class="lnd-hairline" />

<!-- ============ HOW IT RUNS ============ -->
<section class="lnd-section" id="how-it-runs">
    <div class="lnd-wrap">
        <div class="lnd-head" data-reveal>
            <p class="lnd-kicker">02 &mdash; How an engagement runs</p>
            <h2>Four steps, and the same record through all of them.</h2>
            <p>
                The shape below is what the platform enforces. It is also the reason the
                services above can be quoted together: each step hands the next one a client
                file that already exists.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="lnd-ledger" data-reveal>
            <div>
                <span class="lnd-ledger__num">01</span>
                <div>
                    <h3>Scoping</h3>
                    <p>
                        What the ward, the rescue station or the department actually uses, at
                        what rate, and which of it must arrive on a cold chain. This is where
                        the reorder points come from - they are set against consumption, not
                        against a supplier's pack size.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <span class="lnd-ledger__num">02</span>
                <div>
                    <h3>Quotation</h3>
                    <p>
                        Priced lines with lead times, issued as a branded PDF and live in the
                        portal. The client accepts or declines there; the answer is a status on
                        the quotation rather than a reply that has to be chased.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <span class="lnd-ledger__num">03</span>
                <div>
                    <h3>Supply</h3>
                    <p>
                        Stock picked, packed and sent with a tracking reference; or bought in
                        against a purchase order when it is not ours to hold yet. Installations
                        are booked in the same window as the delivery.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <span class="lnd-ledger__num">04</span>
                <div>
                    <h3>Keeping it working</h3>
                    <p>
                        The asset register carries warranty and calibration dates, the
                        preventive calendar works from them, and a fault raised against a unit
                        lands in a queue with a deadline attached.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="lnd-linkrow" data-reveal>
            <a class="lnd-btn lnd-btn--solid" href="/contact">Start with an enquiry &rarr;</a>
            <a class="lnd-btn lnd-btn--ghost" href="/account/register">Request an account</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ CLOSING ============ -->
<section class="lnd-cta">
    <div class="lnd-wrap" data-reveal>
        <p class="lnd-eyebrow">Verichat Quality Projects</p>
        <h2>Tell us what runs low.</h2>
        <p>
            One enquiry covers consumables, equipment, delivery and the service calendar
            behind them. We will price them together or separately, as you use them.
        </p>
        <div class="lnd-cta__actions">
            <a class="lnd-btn lnd-btn--solid" href="/contact">Send an enquiry &rarr;</a>
            <a class="lnd-btn lnd-btn--ghost" href="/about">Who we are</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
